CHAPTER.VERS:
If a man shall sin against his neighbour, and an oath be laid upon him to make him swear, and the oath shall come 
        before thy altar in this house; 

          and an oath…: Heb. and he require an oath of him

And if thy people Israel are defeated by the enemy, because they have sinned against thee; and shall return and confess thy name, and pray and make supplication before thee in this house;
be put…: or, be smitten
in: or, toward

If they sin against thee, (for no man who sinneth not,) and thou be angry with them, and deliver them over before
enemies, and they carry them away captives to a land far off or near;
they carry them away captives: Heb. they that take them captives carry them away
